  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA n2000 (single profile) achieves 0.485 accuracy, clearly outperforming image-only ResNet50 (0.208). This identifies RNA as the dominant modality, so improving RNA is the highest-leverage path. Uncertainty: We have no data on whether multiprofile (multiple profiles per cell) provides additional discriminative signal for RNA, and this is a fundamental design axis that affects a large portion of the remaining search space. This experiment (config_002) isolates the effect of multiprofile + avgpool aggregation on the already-best modality and encoder (PCA n2000), changing only profile_setting and adding a simple aggregation relative to config_001. If multiprofile helps, it validates the entire multiprofile branch and motivates testing transformer aggregation next; if it does not, we can deprioritize multiprofile configurations and focus on encoder improvements (scvi, scgpt). Under a tight budget, this single-variable extension of the current best result maximally reduces uncertainty about a high-impact design choice."
}

